    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a4978a18086df74e915ba8af048de8ad9840571ebc85b3533ceb75c4d97918b0",
      "text": "An early transfer to the airport is followed by a flight to Canaima National Park. You’ll meet the hotel representatives, pay the tax and transfer to the hotel. Lunch follows check-in.\n\nIn the afternoon, cross Canaima Lagoon in a traditional Indigenous canoe known as a curiara. Four waterfalls feed the lagoon: Hacha, Ucaima, Golondrina and Wadaima.\n\nThen walk around the island named for Anatoly, a Russian explorer of the area. One of the day’s highlights is walking behind El Sapo Falls, between the rock face and the curtain of water from the Carrao River. You can swim in the lagoon by the waterfall if you wish.\n\n**Meals:** lunch and dinner.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw8vsjy6-afdp41bp",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
